    "monetize": {
      "question": "How do you want to monetize?",
      "intro": "You've got two strong paths:",
      "paths": [
        {
          "label": "One-time course sales",
          "desc": "for bigger upfront purchases"
        },
        {
          "label": "Subscription access",
          "desc": "for recurring revenue and stronger long-term customer value"
        }
      ],
      "suggestion": "I can recommend the best model for your business if you want."
    },
    "moduleIntro": "I've selected the best modules for your platform. Remove anything you'd like to skip:",
    "logoUpload": {
      "uploading": "Logo uploading…",
      "done": "Logo uploaded.",
      "fileName": "nutrifit-logo.svg",
      "statusUploading": "Uploading...",
      "statusDone": "Uploaded"
    },
    "conversation": [
      "Hey! I'm Admino's AI assistant — your business advisor and platform builder. What do you want to create today?",
      "I'm a certified personal trainer and nutritionist. I want to build a premium online fitness academy with courses, meal plans, and later live sessions, events, and scheduling.",
      "That's a strong niche. You've got expertise, demand, and clear upsell potential. You're building more than a content platform. You're building a premium fitness business.",
      "What do you want to launch first: on-demand content, live sessions, or both?",
      "On-demand first. Live sessions and events can come later.",
      "Smart move. More scalable. Better margins. Once traction builds, you can layer live coaching on top as a premium upsell.",
      "Please do. I'm not very experienced with pricing models.",
      "Then I'd start with subscriptions. Fitness works best with continuity. For fitness and nutrition, subscriptions usually win because your clients don't want one piece of content — they want ongoing guidance, structure, and accountability. That means better retention, more predictable revenue, and more room to introduce new programs over time.",
      "Makes sense. Let's do monthly subscriptions.",
      "I'd recommend a weekly entry plan and an annual plan.",
      "Why those?",
      "Because they do two different jobs brilliantly.\nThe weekly plan lowers friction and gets curious users in fast.\nThe annual plan locks in commitment, improves cash flow, and usually outperforms monthly plans on total revenue.\nIt's a strong combo: low barrier to enter, high incentive to stay.",
      "Perfect. Let's do that.",
      "Great. What's the brand name?",
      "NutriFit Academy.",
      "Strong name. Clean, memorable, and instantly tells people what world they're entering.\nNow give me a rough idea of your early growth target.",
      "Around 10 to 20 users at first. I want to reach 150 by month six.",
      "That's realistic — and healthy. Small early audiences convert best when the platform feels focused, credible, and transformation-oriented.",
      "Based on your business, here's the module stack I'd recommend for NutriFit Academy:",
      "Remove Community.",
      "I can do that — but quick note:\nFor fitness businesses, community often becomes more than a feature. It becomes retention infrastructure. When members feel they're part of something, they stay longer, engage more, and market the brand for you.\nThat said, if your brand promise is more private, premium, and one-to-one, then removing it can actually strengthen positioning.\nDo you want social energy, or private premium guidance?",
      "Private premium guidance. I don't want clients interacting with each other.",
      "Got it.\nThat's a clear brand choice.\nRemoving Community.",
      "Do you already have a logo or should I help create one?",
      "I already have a logo.",
      "Perfect. Upload it and I'll match the platform to your brand.",
      "Logo received. Analyzing now…",
      "Nice — clean typography, strong green palette, premium wellness feel.\nThis brand says: expert-led, modern, results-focused, but still approachable.\nThat gives us a very clear creative direction.",
      "Exactly. I want premium but approachable.",
      "Perfect. I've got the direction. I now have everything I need:\nyour business model, monetization strategy, audience size, module stack, and brand identity.\n\nI'm generating the first platform concept for NutriFit Academy now — built to help you launch fast, look premium, and grow into live coaching when you're ready.\n\nLet's go."
    ]
  },
